WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:05.467
The Chao Phraya River
carries centuries of memory.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.900
In 1782, a new royal capital took root.

3
00:00:11.233 --> 00:00:16.367
In 1782, the Chakri
dynasty began its reign.

4
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:21.833
King Rama I founded the city
on Rattanakosin Island.

5
00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:27.267
The Grand Palace rose
as the majestic throne.

6
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.733
Wat Arun illuminated the
dawn across the river.

7
00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:38.167
Canals branched from
the Chao Phraya River.

8
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.633
Wat Pho preserved sacred
Buddhist traditions.

9
00:00:43.967 --> 00:00:49.100
The Grand Palace sparkled
with sacred emerald.

10
00:00:49.433 --> 00:00:54.533
Wat Pho housed the
world-renowned gilded Buddha.

11
00:00:54.867 --> 00:01:00.000
The Chao Phraya River
became a bustling corridor.

12
00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:05.467
Wat Arun towered above the river sunset.

13
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:10.900
The Chao Phraya River
tested the city in floods.

14
00:01:11.233 --> 00:01:16.367
The Grand Palace stood
resolute through storms.

15
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:21.833
Wat Pho provided peace
and enduring shelter.

16
00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:27.267
Wat Arun heralded a new dawn of rebirth.

17
00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:32.733
The Chao Phraya River
links past and present.

18
00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:38.167
The Grand Palace welcomes
travelers from every land.

19
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:43.633
Wat Pho preserves world
cultural wisdom today.

20
00:01:43.967 --> 00:01:49.100
King Rama I gifted an everlasting capital.

21
00:01:49.433 --> 00:01:54.533
The Chao Phraya River
flows onward into forever.

22
00:01:54.867 --> 00:01:54.533
In 1782, Bangkok began its eternal story.
